rowth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=5y(20-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100942 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a46e688b-117f-5394-bcbb-fbfb7a5b6c7b" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Logistic Growth Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c7ca84a-cf9f-50f8-b341-b5cad100965c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-0.6P(700\\,000+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523411} {:answer/id #uuid "6ee52ea6-c780-5145-af3b-00bf2afb2de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=700\\,000P(0.6-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523481} {:answer/id #uuid "b251d084-9823-5f88-b5bc-44200f475b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=700\\,000P(0.6+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523630} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb1b6f5-2157-5ffa-857f-384cd5652759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P(700\\,000-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523684} {:answer/id #uuid "cedd52a2-345c-58b2-928e-6c0218a680ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P(700\\,000+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdb1b6f5-2157-5ffa-857f-384cd5652759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P(700\\,000-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523684} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33bf6b7-b2a2-5c1d-93df-e2640b2be937" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f74431a-7f46-5af6-affc-22cbe39ff9ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-83865" :question/problem "An influenza epidemic is spreading through a community of $700\\,000$ people. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ infected with the flu is jointly proportional to the number of people who have the flu at time $t,$ measured in days,  and the number of uninfected people. If the constant of proportionality is $0.6,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the growth rate of infected people is *jointly* proportional to the number of people who have the flu at time $t,$ and the number of uninfected people, the number of infected people follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.6,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=700\\,000.$ Therefore, the number of people who have the flu is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P(700\\,000-P).\n$$"}]}
